    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nAfter upgrading to 3.3.0, I've started getting crashes with some compiled python code.\n\nAfter compiling with debug symbols, I find that the crash is centred on the following C code:\n\n```c\n  /* \"lib/foo.py\":242\n *             <snip>\n *\n *         part = offset = 0             # <<<<<<<<<<<<<<\n *         <snip>\n *         <snip>\n*/\n  __Pyx_INCREF(__pyx_mstate_global->__pyx_int_0);\n  __Pyx_XDECREF_SET(__pyx_v_part, __pyx_mstate_global->__pyx_int_0);\n\n  __pyx_v_offset = ((PyObject*)0);\n```\n\nwhich then gets used later on, and predictably, crashes horribly\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\nMinimal reproducer:\n\n```cython\ndef do_stuff():\n    mapping: dict[int, int] = {}\n    for line_number, _content in enumerate([]):\n        part = line_number\n\n    part = offset = 0\n\n    for address in range(0, 1):\n        if line_number := mapping.get(address):\n            part = line_number\n            offset = part\n            print(offset)\n```\n\n```shell\nuv run cython -o test.c test.py\n```\n\nAnd have a look at the generated c code.\n\n(and obviously if you were to attempt to run this, it would segfault due to the null dereference)\n\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nCode should work as expected and not try to dereference a null object. Further reductions get the expected\n\n```c\n  __Pyx_INCREF(__pyx_mstate_global->__pyx_int_0);\n  __Pyx_XDECREF_SET(__pyx_v_part, __pyx_mstate_global->__pyx_int_0);\n  __Pyx_INCREF(__pyx_mstate_global->__pyx_int_0);\n  __pyx_v_offset = __pyx_mstate_global->__pyx_int_0;\n```\n\nor\n\n```c\n  __Pyx_INCREF(__pyx_mstate_global->__pyx_int_0);\n  __Pyx_XDECREF_SET(__pyx_v_part, __pyx_mstate_global->__pyx_int_0);\n  __pyx_v_offset = 0;\n```\n\napparently depending on how the type resolver manages things\n\nSo possibly there's some confusion going on about what to do when the type is determined when not?\n\n### OS\n\nLinux & Windows\n\n### Python version\n\n3.14.4\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.3.0\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_",
