            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> it's a change in type inference exposing an existing bug\n\nRight, the return type of the `.get()` method was declared in that commit, which changes the set of assigned types for `line_number` and subsequently `part`.\n\n`line_number` gets correctly inferred as Python `int` due to the assignment from `mapping.get()`. This lets `part` and `offset` correctly get inferred as Python `int`, but the value on the right hand side of the cascaded assignment doesn't get adapted because we end up with two target types, `object` and `int`. Obviously not contradicting and simple to resolve, but we don't resolve it, currently. I'll see what I can come up with.",
